<script>(function(){var P=[["Battle of Kosovo","/battle/battle-of-kosovo","Battle","15 June 1389","An Ottoman army under Sultan Murad I fought an army led by the Serbian Prince Lazar Hrebeljanović on the Kosovo field in 1389; both leaders died, both armies were badly weakened, and the Serbian principalities later became Ottoman vassals."],["Battle of Nagashino","/battle/battle-of-nagashino","Battle","29 June 1575","In June 1575 the allied armies of Oda Nobunaga and Tokugawa Ieyasu defeated Takeda Katsuyori's army near Nagashino Castle in Mikawa Province, Japan, killing many Takeda generals and making Nobunaga's unification of Japan seem certain."],["Battle of Shanghai","/battle/battle-of-shanghai","Battle","13 August – 26 November 1937","China's National Revolutionary Army and Japan's Imperial Army fought for Shanghai from August to November 1937, in the Second Sino-Japanese War; Japan took the city at heavy cost to both sides and advanced on Nanjing."],["Battle of Uhud","/battle/battle-of-uhud","Battle","23 March 625","The Quraysh of Mecca under Abu Sufyan ibn Harb fought the early Muslims under Muhammad near Mount Uhud, north of Medina, in March 625; the Muslims lost heavily after part of their archer force left its hill, and the Meccans withdrew without pressing on."],["Battle of the Hydaspes","/battle/battle-of-the-hydaspes","Battle","May 326 BCE","Alexander the Great's Macedonian army crossed the swollen Hydaspes in May 326 BCE and defeated the Pauravas under Porus on its bank in what is now Punjab, Pakistan; Alexander spared Porus and made him a satrap."],["Battle of Salamis","/battle/battle-of-salamis","Battle","480 BCE","An Allied Greek fleet under Themistocles defeated a larger Achaemenid fleet under King Xerxes in the straits between the island of Salamis and the mainland in 480 BCE, after which Xerxes withdrew with much of his army."],["Battle of Gaugamela","/battle/battle-of-gaugamela","Battle","1 October 331 BCE","Alexander the Great and the army of Macedon defeated the Persian army of Darius III at Gaugamela, north of Arbela in what is now Iraq, in 331 BCE; the Achaemenid Empire fell soon after."],["Battle of Pydna","/battle/battle-of-pydna","Battle","22 June 168 BCE","Roman legions under the consul Lucius Aemilius Paullus defeated King Perseus of Macedon and his phalanx near Pydna in 168 BCE, in the Third Macedonian War, ending the Antigonid line of kings and Macedonian independence."],["Battle of Lepanto","/battle/battle-of-lepanto","Battle","7 October 1571","On 7 October 1571 the Holy League fleet under John of Austria defeated the Ottoman fleet in the Gulf of Patras; the Ottomans rebuilt quickly, and Venice made peace with them in 1573 and gave up Cyprus."],["Normandy landings","/battle/normandy-landings","Battle","6 June 1944","On 6 June 1944 American, British and Canadian forces, with airborne troops and a fleet drawn from eight navies, landed on five beaches on the Normandy coast, opening the liberation of France and Western Europe."],["Battle of Leipzig","/battle/battle-of-leipzig","Battle","16–19 October 1813","The armies of the Sixth Coalition, from Austria, Prussia, Sweden and Russia, defeated Napoleon's Grande Armée at Leipzig in Saxony over four days in October 1813, and the French withdrew to France."],["Battle of Carrhae","/battle/battle-of-carrhae","Battle","9 June 53 BCE","A Parthian cavalry army under Surena defeated the Roman army of Marcus Licinius Crassus near Carrhae in 53 BCE; Crassus was killed, most of his men were killed or captured, and Parthia later invaded Syria and Armenia."],["Battle of the Pyramids","/battle/battle-of-the-pyramids","Battle","21 July 1798","On 21 July 1798 Bonaparte's French army, formed in squares, defeated Murad Bey's Mamluk-led force near Embabeh in Ottoman Egypt, shattering Murad's field army and opening the way to Cairo."],["Battle of the Bulge","/battle/battle-of-the-bulge","Battle","16 December 1944 – 25 January 1945","A German offensive through the Ardennes in Belgium and Luxembourg took the Western Allies by surprise on 16 December 1944 but was halted short of the Meuse, and the front was restored by the end of January 1945."],["Battle of the Nile","/battle/battle-of-the-nile","Battle","1–3 August 1798","A British fleet under Rear-Admiral Sir Horatio Nelson attacked the French fleet of Vice-admiral Brueys anchored in Aboukir Bay, Egypt, in August 1798, and destroyed or captured all but four of its ships, leaving Napoleon's army in Egypt cut off."],["Battle of the Kalka River","/battle/battle-of-the-kalka-river","Battle","31 May 1223","On 31 May 1223 a Mongol force under Jebe and Subutai defeated Cumans and Rus' princes at the Kalka River, in present-day Donetsk Oblast, and then killed the Kievan prince and his nobles after their camp surrendered."],["Battle of Tsushima","/battle/battle-of-tsushima","Battle","27–28 May 1905","In the Tsushima Strait on 27–28 May 1905 the Japanese Combined Fleet under Tōgō Heihachirō destroyed or captured nearly all of the Russian Second Pacific Squadron under Rozhestvensky, and Russia sued for peace that year."],["Second Battle of Panipat","/battle/second-battle-of-panipat","Battle","5 November 1556","On 5 November 1556 the Mughals under the young Akbar and his guardian Bairam Khan defeated Hemchandra Vikramaditya, known as Hemu, at Panipat, after he had taken Delhi and Agra; Hemu was captured and beheaded."],["Third Battle of Panipat","/battle/third-battle-of-panipat","Battle","14 January 1761","On 14 January 1761 the Durrani Empire and its Indian allies defeated the Maratha army at Panipat, 97 kilometres north of Delhi; tens of thousands of Marathas died in the fighting and after it."],["Battle of Yamen","/battle/battle-of-yamen","Battle","19 March 1279","A Yuan fleet under Zhang Hongfan defeated the chained Song fleet in the bay at Yamen in southern China on 19 March 1279, ending the Song dynasty; the child emperor Zhao Bing died in the sea."],["Battle of Navarino","/battle/battle-of-navarino","Battle","20 October 1827","A British, French and Russian fleet under Admiral Codrington defeated and largely destroyed an Ottoman and Egyptian fleet at anchor in Navarino Bay in 1827, during the Greek War of Independence, which made Greek independence much more likely."],["Battle of Adrianople","/battle/battle-of-adrianople","Battle","9 August 378","Gothic rebels under Fritigern defeated the Eastern Roman army and killed the emperor Valens near Adrianople in Thrace in 378, during the Gothic War of 376 to 382."],["Battle of Gettysburg","/battle/battle-of-gettysburg","Battle","1 to 3 July 1863","Union forces under George Meade defeated Robert E. Lee's Confederate army at Gettysburg, Pennsylvania, from 1 to 3 July 1863, ending Lee's invasion of the North and forcing his retreat to Virginia."],["Battle of Caporetto","/battle/battle-of-caporetto","Battle","24 October – 19 November 1917","Austro-Hungarian forces reinforced by German units broke through the Italian line near Kobarid on the Isonzo front in October 1917, routed the Italian Second Army and drove the Italian army back to the Piave river."],["Battle of Ayacucho","/battle/battle-of-ayacucho","Battle","9 December 1824","On the Pampa de Ayacucho in the Peruvian highlands, Antonio José de Sucre's United Liberation Army defeated the royalist army of Viceroy José de la Serna, who was wounded and captured, and the royalists capitulated, ending Spanish rule in Peru."],["Battle of Guandu","/battle/battle-of-guandu","Battle","200 CE","In 200 CE, late in the Eastern Han dynasty, the warlord Cao Cao held the fortified camp at Guandu against the larger army of Yuan Shao, burned Yuan's grain at Wuchao and routed him, becoming the dominant power in northern China."],["Fall of Constantinople","/battle/fall-of-constantinople","Battle","6 April to 29 May 1453","The Ottoman army under Sultan Mehmed II besieged Constantinople for 53 days and took the Byzantine capital on 29 May 1453, after which the city was sacked and became the Ottoman capital; the fate of Emperor Constantine XI is unknown."],["Battle of Vienna (1683)","/battle/battle-of-vienna-1683","Battle","12 September 1683","On 12 September 1683 a relief army of Imperial and Polish forces under John III Sobieski defeated the Ottoman army of Kara Mustafa Pasha at Vienna, after a two-month siege, and the Ottomans were later driven from most of Hungary."],["Battle of Austerlitz","/battle/battle-of-austerlitz","Battle","2 December 1805","Napoleon's Grande Armée defeated a combined Russian and Austrian army near Austerlitz in Moravia on 2 December 1805, in the War of the Third Coalition, and Austria then left the war by the Treaty of Pressburg."],["Battle of Trafalgar","/battle/battle-of-trafalgar","Battle","21 October 1805","A British fleet under Vice-Admiral Nelson defeated a combined French and Spanish fleet under Villeneuve off Cape Trafalgar in 1805, losing no ship, though Nelson was killed; Britain's command of the sea was not tested for over a century."],["Battle of Issus","/battle/battle-of-issus","Battle","5 November 333 BCE","Alexander the Great's Hellenic League army defeated the Achaemenid army of Darius III near the Pinarus river by Issus in southern Anatolia in 333 BCE, and Darius fled, leaving his family and treasury to be captured."],["Battle of Isandlwana","/battle/battle-of-isandlwana","Battle","22 January 1879","A Zulu army of some 20,000 overran part of the British main column at Isandlwana in Zululand on 22 January 1879, early in the Anglo-Zulu War, killing over 1,300 troops and bringing a larger second British invasion."],["Battle of Crécy","/battle/battle-of-crecy","Battle","26 August 1346","An English army under Edward III, standing on a hillside near Crécy-en-Ponthieu in northern France, beat off repeated attacks by a much larger French army under Philip VI in 1346, during the Hundred Years' War, and went on to take Calais."],["Battle of Verdun","/battle/battle-of-verdun","Battle","21 February – 18 December 1916","The German 5th Army attacked the French defences at Verdun on the Western Front in 1916 to draw in and wear down the French army; after 302 days the French had recovered most of the ground and the Germans had failed to reach their aim."],["Fall of Singapore","/battle/fall-of-singapore","Battle","8 to 15 February 1942","Japanese forces under General Tomoyuki Yamashita crossed the Johor Strait and took Singapore from the British garrison under Lieutenant-General Arthur Percival, who surrendered on 15 February 1942 in the Second World War."],["Battle of Dien Bien Phu","/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu","Battle","13 March – 7 May 1954","Viet Minh forces under Võ Nguyên Giáp besieged and overran a French Union garrison in the valley of Điện Biên Phủ in northwest Tonkin in 1954, in the First Indochina War, and French withdrawal from Indochina followed."],["Battle of Warsaw (1920)","/battle/battle-of-warsaw-1920","Battle","August 1920","In August 1920, during the Polish–Soviet War, a Polish counterattack under Józef Piłsudski broke Mikhail Tukhachevsky's Red Army advance on Warsaw and drove it eastward, and a treaty in 1921 fixed Poland's eastern frontier."],["Battle of Puebla","/battle/battle-of-puebla","Battle","5 May 1862","French troops under Charles de Lorencez failed three times to storm the Mexican forts of Loreto and Guadalupe above Puebla on 5 May 1862, during the second French intervention in Mexico, and withdrew to Orizaba to await reinforcements."],["Battle of Marignano","/battle/battle-of-marignano","Battle","13–14 September 1515","Francis I of France, with German landsknechts and late-arriving Venetian allies, defeated the Swiss Confederacy near Melegnano, south-east of Milan, in September 1515; the Perpetual Peace of 1516 followed."],["Battle of Zama","/battle/battle-of-zama","Battle","202 BCE","A Roman army under Scipio Africanus defeated a Carthaginian army under Hannibal near Zama in what is now Tunisia in 202 BCE, ending the Second Punic War and leaving Carthage politically subordinate to Rome."],["Battle of Sekigahara","/battle/battle-of-sekigahara","Battle","21 October 1600 (Keichō 5, 15th day of the 9th month)","On 21 October 1600 the forces of Tokugawa Ieyasu defeated a coalition led by Ishida Mitsunari in what is now Gifu Prefecture after several commanders defected; Ieyasu became shōgun in 1603."],["Battle of the Catalaunian Plains","/battle/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains","Battle","20 June 451 CE","A coalition led by the Roman general Aetius and the Visigothic king Theodoric I fought the Huns and their vassals under Attila in Gaul in 451 CE; Theodoric was killed, Attila withdrew, and the outcome is disputed."],["Battle of Sagrajas","/battle/battle-of-sagrajas","Battle","23 October 1086","An Almoravid army under Yusuf ibn Tashfin, joined by the taifa kings of al-Andalus, defeated Alfonso VI of Castile near Badajoz in October 1086, easing Christian pressure on the taifas and opening the way for Almoravid rule in al-Andalus."],["Battle of Karbala","/battle/battle-of-karbala","Battle","10 October 680","On 10 October 680 at Karbala in southern Iraq, the army of the Umayyad caliph Yazid I killed Husayn ibn Ali, grandson of Muhammad, and most of his small party, with consequences for the Second Fitna and for Shia identity."],["Battle of Stalingrad","/battle/battle-of-stalingrad","Battle","17 July 1942 – 2 February 1943","The Soviet Union defeated Germany and its Axis allies at Stalingrad on the Volga between 1942 and 1943; the German 6th Army was encircled and surrendered, and the strategic initiative on the Eastern Front passed to the Red Army."],["First Battle of the Marne","/battle/first-battle-of-the-marne","Battle","5 to 12 September 1914","French and British armies under Joffre counter-attacked the German right wing between Paris and Verdun in September 1914, forced the Germans to retreat to the Aisne and ended the German plan for a quick victory in the west."],["Battle of Kadesh","/battle/battle-of-kadesh","Battle","May 1274 BCE","Ramesses II of Egypt and Muwatalli II of the Hittite Empire fought on the Orontes near Kadesh after a Hittite attack nearly broke the Egyptian army; both sides claimed victory and the Hittites kept Kadesh."],["Battle of the Trebia","/battle/battle-of-the-trebia","Battle","22 or 23 December 218 BCE","Hannibal's Carthaginian army lured a Roman army under the consul Sempronius Longus across the icy Trebia near Placentia in December 218 BCE, in the first major battle of the Second Punic War, and defeated it heavily."],["Battle of Kursk","/battle/battle-of-kursk","Battle","5 July – 23 August 1943","In the summer of 1943 German forces attacked the Kursk salient on the Eastern Front, were stopped by deep Soviet defences, and were then driven back by Soviet counter-offensives that left the Red Army holding the strategic initiative."],["Battle of Marengo","/battle/battle-of-marengo","Battle","14 June 1800","French forces under the First Consul Napoleon Bonaparte beat Michael von Melas's Austrian army near Alessandria in Piedmont on 14 June 1800 after a near defeat, and the Austrians left north-western Italy."],["Battle of Kulikovo","/battle/battle-of-kulikovo","Battle","8 September 1380","On 8 September 1380 the Russian forces of Grand Prince Dmitry of Moscow defeated the army of Mamai of the Golden Horde at Kulikovo Field near the Don, though Mongol overlordship over Russia went on."],["Battle of Badr","/battle/battle-of-badr","Battle","13 March 624 CE","On 13 March 624 CE (17 Ramadan, 2 AH) Muhammad's followers from Medina defeated a larger Qurayshi army from Mecca near Badr, killing several Meccan leaders and strengthening Muhammad's position."],["Battle of Alarcos","/battle/battle-of-alarcos","Battle","18 July 1195","The Almohad caliph Abu Yusuf Ya'qub al-Mansur defeated King Alfonso VIII of Castile at Alarcos, near the Guadiana, on 18 July 1195, and Castile's field army was destroyed, leaving the road to Toledo open."],["Battle of Thapsus","/battle/battle-of-thapsus","Battle","6 April 46 BCE","Julius Caesar's army defeated the Optimate forces of Quintus Caecilius Metellus Scipio and King Juba I of Numidia near Thapsus in North Africa on 6 April 46 BCE, in the last civil war of the Roman Republic."],["Siege of Baghdad (1258)","/battle/siege-of-baghdad-1258","Battle","January–February 1258","A Mongol army under Hulegu besieged Baghdad, capital of the Abbasid Caliphate, in early 1258; the city surrendered on 10 February, was sacked and the caliph al-Musta'sim was executed, ending the caliphate there."],["Battle of Manzikert","/battle/battle-of-manzikert","Battle","26 August 1071","On 26 August 1071 the Seljuk army of Alp Arslan defeated the Byzantine army of Romanos IV Diogenes near Manzikert in eastern Anatolia and captured the emperor, and civil strife in Byzantium followed."],["Battle of Kohima","/battle/battle-of-kohima","Battle","4 April – 22 June 1944","A British and Indian garrison held Kohima ridge against the Japanese 31st Division in April 1944, was relieved, and with reinforcements drove the Japanese off, reopening the road to Imphal in June."],["Battle of Madagascar","/battle/battle-of-madagascar","Battle","5 May – 6 November 1942","British and Allied forces landed at Diego-Suarez on 5 May 1942 and then took the rest of the Vichy French-held island of Madagascar, to keep Japanese ships from its ports; an armistice came on 6 November."],["Battle of Hattin","/battle/battle-of-hattin","Battle","4 July 1187","On 4 July 1187 the army of the Crusader states, under King Guy of Jerusalem, was surrounded and broken near Tiberias by Saladin's forces, which then took Jerusalem and most Crusader-held towns and prompted the Third Crusade."],["Fall of Tenochtitlan","/battle/fall-of-tenochtitlan","Battle","May – 13 August 1521","A Spanish force under Hernán Cortés and tens of thousands of Indigenous allies, above all Tlaxcalans, besieged the Mexica capital Tenochtitlan in 1521, starved it, and took it on 13 August, after which the city was sacked."]],d=Math.floor(Date.now()/864e5),p=P[d%P.length],a=document.getElementById("hub-pick");if(a){a.href=p[1];var im=document.createElement("img");im.src="/logos/thumbs/"+encodeURIComponent(p[0]).replace(/'/g,"%27")+".png";im.alt="";im.width=64;im.height=64;a.querySelector(".hub-pick-img").appendChild(im);a.querySelector(".hub-pick-k").textContent="Today\u2019s pick \u00b7 "+p[2]+(p[3]?" \u00b7 "+p[3]:"");a.querySelector(".hub-pick-n").textContent=p[0];a.querySelector(".hub-pick-d").textContent=p[4];}var b=document.getElementById("hub-surprise"),P=["/battle/"];if(b)b.addEventListener("click",function(){function go(){if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES==="undefined")return;var a=SEARCH_PROFILES.filter(function(r){return P.some(function(p){return r[1].indexOf(p)===0})});if(a.length)location.href=a[Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length)][1]}if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES!=="undefined")return go();var sc=document.createElement("script");sc.src=(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC!=="undefined"?SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC:"/search-profiles.js");sc.onload=go;sc.onerror=go;document.head.appendChild(sc)});})();</script>
